# p_b2e9 — Weekend both-home: shared kitchen mornings, both items at the entry, no work

On weekends neither resident is at work, so the entire set of personal items—jackets, keys, helmets, bike locks, bags—remains in the house. Both jackets hang at the entry hook; both sets of keys and both bike locks sit on the entry table. In the morning the pair share the kitchen: the kettle is on the counter, mugs are at the kitchen table, and both residents are present in the room. Midday may bring a brief errand, but the items return to the entry by the afternoon. Omar's tablet and both phones stay at the bedroom nightstand overnight and through the morning, matching the Saturday-00:00 sighting that placed both phones at the nightstand rather than the coffee table.

What sets this apart from the weekday "both drive" documents (p_4e91, p_a3f7, p_e9b3): those documents still assume one resident is out during part of the day, so one set of entry items would be missing. Here, every item is in the house all day. The morning kitchen use is shared (both mugs at the table) rather than staggered.

What would refute it: if a jacket, key set, or bike lock is consistently absent from the entry on a weekend; if only one mug is at the kitchen table during the morning; if Omar's tablet is found at the kitchen chair or coffee table rather than the nightstand on a weekend morning.

